// "DealsDamageToEach" — the mass-burn / board-wipe damage shape (the
// damage-sweeper family): an object deals damage ([CR#120.1]) to every
// member of a recipient class at once ([CR#608.2d] distributive each —
// iterating a many-`Binder` binds each selected object in turn as the
// anaphor `It`). Pyroclasm's "~ deals 2 damage to each creature.", Flame
// Rift's "each player", Hour of Devastation's "each opponent", and any other
// characteristic-filtered recipient ("each creature your opponents
// control") all ride this one macro — the migrations parser's
// `parse_deal_damage`/`damage_target` production reads the recipient-class
// phrase (via the shared object-target filter grammar) and emits this
// invocation with that filter as the second argument, since the generic
// macro-template fallthrough can't itself synthesize an arbitrary
// `Predicate` from English.
//
// `source` is fixed at `This` — every corpus usage is a spell/ability
// naming its own source ("~ deals …"), never a foreign dealer; a card that
// needs a different source is a distinct (unbuilt) shape.
//
// Usage: DealsDamageToEach(2, Creature) / DealsDamageToEach(1,
// OpponentOf(Ref(You))) / DealsDamageToEach(3, And([Creature,
// ControlledBy(OpponentOf(Ref(You)))])).
(
    name: "DealsDamageToEach",
    template: "~ deals ${0} damage to each ${1}",
    kinds: [OneShotEffect],
    params: [Count, Predicate],
    frames: ["~ deals <Param(0)> damage to each <Param(1)>"],
    body: Each(binder: Existing(SelectAll(Param(1))), effect: DealDamage(This, Param(0), It)),
)
